From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: wait for a NIC's IRQ only on that NIC's own event

40-net-smp-affinity ran its whole body on every net "add" event, for
whatever device appeared: each bridge, veth or tunnel waited up to ten
seconds per NIC for that NIC's IRQ to show up in /proc/interrupts. As
procd runs hotplug scripts one after another, a NIC whose IRQ carries
another name held up every other net event behind it for that long.

Wait for a NIC's IRQ only when that NIC itself is added. Any other net
event still sets the affinity of every NIC whose IRQ is there already,
without waiting: a NIC's driver may request its IRQ only when the NIC
is brought up, as r8169 and stmmac do, which can be after the NIC's own
event stopped waiting, and the next net device to appear then sets it,
as before.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../armv8/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/40-net-smp-affinity  | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/rockchip/armv8/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/40-net-smp-affinity b/target/linux/rockchip/armv8/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/40-net-smp-affinity
index 4d734e5..fd46068 100644
--- a/target/linux/rockchip/armv8/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/40-net-smp-affinity
+++ b/target/linux/rockchip/armv8/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/40-net-smp-affinity
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ set_interface_core() {
 
 	[ -z "${device}" ] && device="$interface"
 
+	# Wait for the IRQ only when this interface itself appears. Any other
+	# net device (a bridge, a veth, a tunnel) sets the affinity only if the
+	# IRQ is there already.
+	[ "${INTERFACE}" = "${interface}" ] ||
+		grep -q -E "${device}\$" /proc/interrupts || return 0
+
 	local irq=$(get_device_irq "$device")
 
 	echo "${core_mask}" > /proc/irq/${irq}/smp_affinity
